{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939154-summoning-supernal-entities-how-often-does-this-come-up","id":939154,"title":"Summoning Supernal Entities: How Often does this come up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-28T14:46:20-07:00","id":939154,"title":"Summoning Supernal Entities: How Often does this come up?","content":"I am struggling to get my head around how frequently mages make use of their ability to conjure Supernal Entities. In 1e we only found out about it in the Summoners sourcebook and my take on it then was that it was a rare, esoteric discipline, the type of thing mages quested after to discover the necessary techniques in order to further some greater goal. I am totally open to the possibility of this new interpretation, hell I love the drama and tension of a big occult summoning scene! Its just now its smack bang in the middle of the Core book I am unsure just how frequently its meant to come up?<br /> <br /> Do NPC mages in your games conjure and converse with Supernal spirits on a regular basis? How often have your players turned to the higher realms for answers to their questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:10:08-07:00","id":939170,"title":"","content":"In my game, I had an Obsession with my PC that involved summoning an Anachronism from Arcadia, asking it to bring to me the beginning of a conspiracy surrounding his family. It successfully transported to 1920's Melbourne, where I solved mysteries with a Thearch named Phryne. In another instance, an NPC was noted as being a regular Summoner of Atavisms, to collect rare plant variants from large elementals born of various tree mythologies. I place it as being simple enough, but you mustn't ever demand from them. Just ask nicely, and deal with their diva attitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:12:28-07:00","id":939173,"title":"","content":"I think it should still be a rare and momentous event. Although, <i>technically</i>, odds are a great deal of even starting mages could do it (3 dots in one of their Ruling Arcana) is still mechanically and narratively difficult and taxing. One only summons one of these beings with an specific objective in mind, and it always has a step cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:14:15-07:00","id":939174,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say Supernal summoning is something that is, or ever should be, done with any degree of regularity or any sense of the commonplace. It is a thoroughly dangerous action; a slip-up invites an Abyssal manifestation into the world or, worse, sees a Supernal being fed to non-reality. Yes, measures may be taken to prevent this but no guarantee is perfect. This, all before consideration that a Supernal entity in and of itself, even when friendly, may be actively harmful to everyone and everything around it.<br /> <br /> All that said, however, Supernal summoning is far from unheard of in my games. The risk is very much a thing measured against a reward. Supernal entities are glorious and powerful, and can offer insight into the grandest Mysteries of all as no other being can. Even the weakest and most insignificant can be powerful allies far in advance of others.<br /> <br /> One of my Moros players has an ongoing relationship with a Stygian entity known as Gur Aryeh - the Young Lion; the same entity who taught the Maharal how to construct golems with which to defend the Jewish people of Prague - who acts as a frequent advisor on Supernal matters and provides insight into alchemy. The Moros in question doesn't summon him often, but the central importance of the entity to his mystical endeavours have seen him dedicate an entire room in his sanctum to the sole purpose of calling Gur Aryeh. In the past, Gur Aryeh has directed the Necromancer to find his first Hallow; provided him with the location of an ancient alchemist's workshop; guided him to a stockpile of thunderbolt iron; and explained the nature of a Bound. On occasion, Gur Aryeh has provided material aid too, in the form of the occasional Supernal artifact. Every one of these caused the Necromancer to uncover some old, stagnant relic and make it into something new, which is in keeping with Gur Aryeh's transformative nature.<br /> <br /> Supernal entities are powerful and deservedly so, but shouldn't come up <i>too</i> often; they should be treated as the dangerous but awe-inspiring beings they are; even the most familiar treated as a wise mentor atop a high mountain, whose climb is at times risky and dangerous. Calling one down should be a momentous occasion, done when nothing else will satisfy the need for insight only they can offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:09:49-07:00","id":940364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katana1515</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/939154-summoning-supernal-entities-how-often-does-this-come-up#post939154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do NPC mages in your games conjure and converse with Supernal spirits on a regular basis? How often have your players turned to the higher realms for answers to their questions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes and no. The great thing about summoning is, try as you might, you don't quite know who or what will answer your call. We have an Obrimos PC whose Obsession is communicating / interacting with Angels. When he finally succeeded, it was a Rank 2 Cherub named Eblis (Prime / Life) that materialized; a giant raven with six eyes, human hind legs, and claws on his wings. A golden mandala halo shimmered behind its head.<br /> <br /> The thing is, the PC was trying to invoke a higher ranking cherub. Eblis turned out to be a servant only, and a particularly prickly and condescending one at that. (It kept on making snide remarks about humans.) Nevertheless, the angel aided our Obrimos after snacking on the stored Mana in his Demesne.<br /> <br /> We also have an NPC Thyrsus who serves as a herbalist, poisons master, and ally of the group. She has been known to summon plant Atavisms, and keep specimens for study and even trade in the black market. She has performed several summonings in the past, but nothing on a regular or habitual basis. Not only does it risk the attention of the Abyss, it also lays open the Fallen World to the untamed forces of the Primal Wild.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:40:31-07:00","id":940378,"title":"","content":"During the playtest, the antagonist that I picked for Team Time was an Acanthus adept from their future who summoned an Anachronism in order to travel ten years back in time, thanks to that pretty much being the only way one could do so in that version of the rules. This was in order to convince the cabal to &quot;deal with&quot; his earlier self in a hopefully lethal manner, so as to enter the ranks of the Cult of the Doomsday Clock and be counted amongst those outside of time for personal reasons. The cabal also found themselves in discussion with the Anachronism before they knew what it was (appeared as a confused old drunk in a dive bar) and when the puzzle pieces started falling into place they weren't quite sure if the entity wasn't potentially a future version of their patron/antagonist &quot;gone Supernal&quot;.<br /> <br /> It was all wonderfully paradoxical, especially when they decided to actually have a chat with their target, the early version of the patron/antagonist, and all three versions ended up in the same warehouse at once. It's possible that Team Time broke the Time Arcanum and got it massively rewritten, but Dave isn't telling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T18:52:04-07:00","id":940383,"title":"","content":"The abyssal slip up is actually pretty hard to achieve. You can roll Gnosis+Arcanum times in total. You need to roll more than Resolve+Composure before any Abyssal Slip Ups can happen. Our Cabal literally has no single character that even *could* slip up this way, as their Resolve+Composure is higher than their Gnosis+Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T21:37:24-07:00","id":940451,"title":"","content":"There's more than one possible Abyssal slip-up, WHW. Abyssal intrusion can occur, but you can also risk having your summoning circle destroyed. If that happens, the Supernal entity can't get back and you have to work fast to build a bridge to the Supernal before it gets eradicated.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you're only really risk-free when you're at low power and summoning weak entities. More powerful Supernal beings require greater risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:15:54-07:00","id":940476,"title":"","content":"As written in core, there are following ways to provoke Abyssal slip up:<br /> a) You roll more times than your Resolve+Composure (so, in generally, around 4-7 times; if you are smart and ask your Mastigos to get you buffed Resolve or Composure, this can go to 10+), and *then*, your GM rolls your Gnosis every next roll to check if intrusion happens, and even *then*, he needs to accumulate successes equal your Gnosis + Primary Arcanum (so minimum of 4, usually something about 5 or 6). This means that you need to fail summoning for 4 extended roll turns, then roll your Gnosis enough times to gather 4-6 successes, which should take either about 15 or 10 turns of extended roll. Unless you are super unlucky, you will probably either finish the summoning, or flat out run out of extended roll turns to finish it before it can get corrupted.<br /> b) You *decide* to take a Dramatic Failure on a summoning roll.<br /> <br /> More powerful entities don't bring greater risk; they only need more successes to summon. And because you have limited number of turns to summon the entity...<br /> Like, you get minimum of 4 rolls (gnosis 1 + arcanum 3), and maximum of 10 rolls (gnosis 5, arcanum 5) to summon an entity. Even if you are something like Gnosis 3 + Arcanum 3 Summoner with Resolve+Composure total of 4, you *still* only risk two times, and both of these times you roll 3 dice and need to accumulate 6 successes. 6 successes on 6 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-31-2016, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:31:38-07:00","id":940482,"title":"","content":"I was also referring to what happens if a Supernal entity runs out of corpus outside the summoning circle.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, getting super-buffed by a Mastigos isn't always available and, even if it were, I'd probably rule that dice from a spell like that count as an equipment bonus (i.e. not contributing to your effective pool). It helps explain why Mages who are buffed don't automatically become posthuman god-beings, and keep Supernal summoning something that's as risky as intended for everyone, not just people without a Warlock on speed-dial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T22:38:22-07:00","id":940483,"title":"","content":"Even without Mastigos speed dial, your Gnosis 3 Arcanum 3 Mage can literally make this way of risking abyssal slip ups impossible to happen by having Resolve and Composure of 3 each. Something that a lot of characters start with. It's not &quot;risky&quot;. It's &quot;literally impossible&quot;, because you get to roll 6 times, and you start risking abyssal intrusion on the 7th roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T00:50:44-07:00","id":940525,"title":"","content":"Seems to me a way better option here would be to remove the roll cap on Supernal summonings. As it stands, a Gnosis 3, Arcanum 3 Mage is going to average two successes a roll for a total of twelve, putting all but the most basic summons out of reach on an average roll. You could even set the &quot;safe&quot; number of rolls to Gnosis + Arcanum. It has about the same effect.<br /> <br /> If you can let players keep rolling, though, suddenly the risk of an Abyssal intrusion grows massively because players can take the risk and aim for bigger targets. It definitely fits, too, with the whole &quot;Your reach exceeds your grasp&quot; theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T03:05:03-07:00","id":940552,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I feel that a way to keep summoning past your cap instead of being told to drop it because extended actions says so would be interesting. Current strategy for doing the summons is to get as many target success removers as possible - which pretty much boils down to &quot;summon in a demesne, roll the hell out of your Intelligence+Occult&quot;. ProTraining in Occult, especially at 5, makes really big difference in Summoning, maybe little *too big*.<br /> Again, note that this power of Occult to reduce target number success makes Warlocks best Summoners, because they can buff their Resolve/Composure for the Summoning, *and* buff their Intelligence/Occult prior to it to shave off as many successes as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T13:56:09-07:00","id":941387,"title":"","content":"Actually, you don't really need to have Mind to buff your Occult; any arcanum can theoretically add dice or successes to the pool. Fate to find the right books in a library; Prime to detect which symbols work and which don't; Matter to read the resonances in objects; Spirit to communicate with spirits of the appropriate nature and get their advice.<br /> <br /> You get the idea. As long as you can explain it, the spell works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T12:06:29-07:00","id":942887,"title":"","content":"Remember, too, Supernal entities need not be spirits. While I'm unfamiliar with Supernal Summoning's game mechanics, many Supernal beings would be just as solid as any thing in the Fallen World. (Yes, I'm referring to Arcadia; in my games, the Supernal Arcadia and the Arcadia changelings suffer their durances in are one and the same. Heaven was full of beautiful godlike monsters well <i>before</i> the Exarchs showed up. [And besides, <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> handily summarizes how Gentry can exist seemingly without Exarch influence!])","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}